From 8ceb4ae66e2d81344000fae376ac645d29180fc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ParkWardRR <alfa147x@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 18:46:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 24/50] feat: add ECW230v3 + EWS377-FIT board support, fix
 EWS377AP v3 bugs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add candidate board support for two EnGenius sibling SKUs that share
identical AP-HK07 hardware (IPQ8072A) with the validated EWS377AP v3:
- EnGenius ECW230v3 (cloud-managed AP, product_id 0x011c)
- EnGenius EWS377-FIT (FIT-controller AP, product_id 0x012c)

No hardware access to these boards — candidate support for community
testing. WiFi board data extracted from stock firmware.

Factor EWS377AP v3 DTS into shared ipq8072-engenius-ap-hk07.dtsi with
thin per-device .dts wrappers (upstream sibling-SKU playbook pattern).

Fix two EWS377AP v3 bugs:
- Add missing ubi.block=0,rootfs bootarg for UBI block device creation
- Add all three EnGenius boards to platform.sh nand_do_upgrade case

Refactor ipq807x.mk to use shared Device/engenius_ap-hk07 base with
IB/INITRAMFS-gated web-ui-factory.fit (matching WAX218 pattern).
